/// Platform application configuration
/// Used by generate-k8s.rb to generate manifests from scala-play-app template
///
/// Load balancer managed via doctl:
///   Name: platform-lb
///   Certificate: idempotent-io-ssl-certificate (a8487391-c0d5-4a33-9ded-408fea25b075)
///   Hostname: idempotent.io
///   Targets: droplets tagged `web-lb-target` (auto-tracks pool replacement)

module platform

appName = "platform"
appPort = 9300
webMemory = "4400Mi"
javaAgent = "/opt/newrelic/newrelic.jar"

// Off for the same reason acumen is, now that the premise has been MEASURED
// rather than assumed. Distributed tracing exists to correlate one request
// across services; the question is whether any trace in this account actually
// does, and platform is the only place it plausibly could — it is the one
// product here with two instrumented tiers.
//
// It does not. Measured on account 7724695, 2026-08-08 (ISS-1084):
//
//   - 1,070,884 of 1,095,515 transactions over 7 days are trace ENTRY POINTS
//     (`nr.entryPoint IS true`) — 97.8%. A tier called by another tier would
//     show up as a continuation, not as the start of its own trace.
//   - `FROM (SELECT uniqueCount(appName) AS apps FROM Span FACET traceId
//     LIMIT MAX) SELECT max(apps)` returns 1.0 across 5,000 traces. Not one
//     contains spans from more than one application.
//   - The account's Span keyset has no `parent.app` attribute at all, so no
//     span has ever recorded a parent in another entity.
//
// That is the architecture, not a sampling artifact: platform-web serves
// requests and platform-job drains a database task queue, and a queue does not
// carry trace context across the hop by design. So every trace begins and ends
// inside one process, which is exactly the case k8s/apps/acumen.pkl turned this
// off for — decided there on the general argument, and confirmed here on the
// numbers.
//
// What it costs, at 40% of the bill. TracingBytes ran 0.87-1.52 GB/day over the
// 14 days to 2026-08-08 against a 2.80 GB/day total, and August projected
// 87.2 GB of a 100 GB free-tier ceiling with acumen not yet reporting at all.
// Without it the run rate is ~1.6 GB/day, or roughly half the ceiling, which is
// what buys room for acumen's two apps and for the ~+5 GB/month the account has
// trended at since March (51.6, 51.5, 60.5, 61.5, 73.5).
//
// What survives, and it is what anything here actually reads: TransactionError
// keeps the class, message and stack trace (0.005 GB across all of platform in
// the same window) so `daily-error-triage` is untouched; transaction traces keep
// per-segment timing for the slowest transactions, since they are an APM
// mechanism rather than a span one; and slow queries are tracked by
// `dev queries top` out of platform's own database, not out of spans.
//
// Flip this back to true (one line, no other change) if platform grows a
// synchronous hop between two instrumented services. Re-check the premise with
// the maxApps query above before doing it — the finding, not the setting, is
// what should decide.
distributedTracing = false
